# Ensembl Go
#
# These rules mirror the exclusions in scripts/archive_github_snapshot.sh, which
# defines what belongs in a distributable source snapshot. Keep the two in step:
# if something is added here, consider whether the snapshot should skip it too.

# --- OS and editor noise ---
.DS_Store
*~
*.bak
*_bak
*.swp

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.tox/

# --- Node ---
node_modules/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vite/
.vite-temp/
coverage/

# --- Build output (all regenerable) ---
frontend/dist/
electron/dist/
electron/dist_backend/
electron/build_backend/
electron/build_log*.txt
# Staged MAFFT bundle, rebuilt by `npm run prepare:mafft`. Everything else under
# electron/build/ (icons, entitlements) is source and must stay tracked.
electron/build/mafft_bin/

# --- Runtime state ---
backend/cache/
backend/output_dir/
backend/local_data/
backend/debug_backend.txt

# --- Genome data does not belong in backend/data ---
# The application ships no sample genomes: users download assemblies through the
# download view or supply their own. backend/data holds only the classification
# artifacts that decide species grouping, which ARE tracked (a couple of megabytes,
# read at run time by backend/project_classifier.py and backend/taxonomy_classifier.py).
# These patterns are a guard, so a stray FASTA or GFF3 left in that directory during
# development cannot be committed or bundled by build-backend.js.
backend/data/*.fa
backend/data/*.fai
backend/data/*.gff3
backend/data/*.gz

# --- Experimental Rust/WASM renderer ---
# The Cargo project and its prebuilt pkg/ output stay tracked; only the build
# directory is ignored, at roughly 790 MB.
frontend/rust/*/target/

# --- Snapshots, vendored clones, scratch ---
exports/
temp_repos/
ensembl_local_github_*/

# --- Local tooling config ---
# Personal settings. A shared .claude/settings.json, if added, should be tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
